From: Yuya Hamamachi <yuya.hamamachi.sx@renesas.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: renesas: r8a779g0: Do not depend on machine compatible for DSC fixup

The DSC clock force-on workaround is skipped unless the root node is
compatible with "renesas,r8a779g0". A Xen guest (DomD) sees the root
compatible of "xen,xenvm", so the workaround never runs there. DSC then
stays off at boot, is not marked CLK_IS_CRITICAL (crit_mod_clks are only
marked critical when on at boot) and DSI1 outputs no video.

This function is only called from the r8a779g0 CPG init, so check the
CPG node compatible instead of the machine compatible.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [temporary workaround, superseded by proper DSC support]
Signed-off-by: Yuya Hamamachi <yuya.hamamachi.sx@renesas.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/renesas/r8a779g0-cpg-mssr.c b/drivers/clk/renesas/r8a779g0-cpg-mssr.c
index 23e588b435b8..b1f35df38b04 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/renesas/r8a779g0-cpg-mssr.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/renesas/r8a779g0-cpg-mssr.c
@@ -355,7 +355,7 @@ static void __init r8a779g0_cpg_mssr_dsc_fixup_init(struct device *dev)
 	u32 value;
 	int error;
 
-	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("renesas,r8a779g0"))
+	if (!of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "renesas,r8a779g0-cpg-mssr"))
 		return;
 
 	dsi1np = of_find_node_by_path("/soc/display@feb00000");
